ict each other red and green  which itself is a complex of yellow and  blue as we know right what do they  produce they produce Brown so Brown  would be like the anger in this case  what about the third argument that was  given here  um  anger involves you know multiple other  emotions and uh Thomas is going to say  yeah I've already addressed that it's  there's a concurrence of multiple causes  here anger involves a number of emotions  not as a Genus does a species so it's  not including all these emotions under  anger but rather as an effect embodies  or includes or is derived from its cause  so it includes these other emotions  which he's naming off you know pain or  sadness  tristia in this case hope and pleasure  or or Delight right so anger can in fact  be rightly understood as a specific  emotion but as one that is produced by  it incorporates other emotions
 

